  "context_markdown": "This public register records known, intentional differences between the supplied printed source and the current edition. The choices are adopted for this edition; they do not purport to recover the original transcriber’s intentions.\n\nAll 18 pages of the source and all four staves received a page/system comparison, with magnified checks of identified passages and native score inspection. This is not an independent second note-by-note transcription or a collation of all surviving sources. The supplied source is the Breitkopf & Härtel collected edition reprinted by Dover, not an autograph.\n\n**Numbering:** the quartet has four musical movements. The catalogue’s five-section record is copied unchanged in the metadata. Movement IV contains La Malinconia (*Adagio*, bars 1–44) and the ensuing *Allegretto*, whose native bar numbering restarts at a pickup and continues 1–252. Entries explicitly name the section and sort Adagio before Allegretto. Movement III uses the native continuous Scherzo/Trio numbering; its pickups and alternate endings are identified where necessary.",
